  "ai_overview": {
    "text_blocks": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "You need a new roof if your asphalt shingle roof is over 20 years old or showing widespread wear from Utah's extreme temperature swings and heavy snow.",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "asphalt shingle roof is over 20 years old or showing widespread wear from Utah's extreme temperature swings and heavy snow"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Warning Signs of Roof Failure"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Advanced Age: Most asphalt roofs in Utah last 18 to 25 years. Extreme UV exposure and freeze-thaw cycles shorten their lifespan compared to milder climates."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Widespread Shingle Damage: Shingles that are curling at the edges, cracking, or breaking apart across large sections mean the material is worn out."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Excessive Granule Loss: Finding a thick layer of dark, sand-like grit in your gutters means your shingles are losing their protective coating and breaking down."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Sagging or Uneven Rooflines: A wavy or drooping roof deck points to rotting structural supports or moisture damage in the wooden decking underneath."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Daylight in the Attic: Seeing pinpricks or beams of daylight coming through your roof boards means the decking has major gaps or holes."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Frequent Interior Leaks: Water stains on your ceiling or walls that keep returning or appear in new spots indicate the entire roof system is failing."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Heavy Moss Growth: Thick green patches trap moisture against the shingles and accelerate decay, especially on shaded north-facing slopes."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Preventing Further Damage"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Inspect safely from the ground using binoculars or check your attic on a sunny day with the lights off."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Avoid overlays because Utah building codes allow a maximum of two shingle layers, but adding a second layer traps heat and hides underlying deck rot."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Consult professionals to get a precise evaluation before winter ice dams cause extensive water damage."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you'd like, tell me:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "How old your roof is"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "What specific damage you see (granules, leaks, curling)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "I can help you decide whether a repair or a full replacement is best."
      }
    ],
